SM(260,{"n":"Genesis 29.30-31.55","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Genesis 29.30-31.55.mp3","d":2642.2,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.08,"Verse 31, but when the Lord saw Leah was hated, he opened her womb, but Rachel was barren."],[30.72,"So this is God stepping in already to work on making this situation right."],[39.3,"Because what's if you're a woman like Leah, Leah had no say in any of this."],[47.76,"Like, none of this is Leah's idea."],[51.69,"And she's now, for the rest of her life, in this marriage with this guy who doesn't love her. her, who's also married to sister, who he does love"],[63.66,"Not a great spot for her to be in as a woman."],[67.66,"But in the ancient world, the hope of the security you have is you have kids, in particular, you have sons."],[78.96,"Especially if you have the firstborn son."],[81.68,"Because he's the one who's going to inherit everything when the husband dies."],[87.02,"And you're his mom, he's going to secure your future."],[91.68,"So she's been placed in this situation."],[94.64,"God blesses her with children."],[97.45,"Sort of as as recompense."],[100.95,"And hypothetically, Jacob might have looked at this situation, where Leah is having children, and Rachel is not."],[111.19,"This might have communicated something to him about how he was treating them."],[122.37,"It could have within that."],[124.05,"And of course, notice for her to be having these children, he is sleeping with her."],[130.93,"So I mean, he's not that appalled by her, clearly."],[142.58,"So Leah conceived and bore Jacob a son, and she called his name Reuben"],[148.3,"For she said, The Lord has surely looked on my humiliation."],[151.9,"Now therefore my husband will love me."],[155.66,"That's depressing and sad."],[157.66,"Yes. Oh, now I've had his firstborn son, so now he'll love me."],[163.75,"Kinda kinda sad."],[165.43,"What is Reuben's name?"],[168.31,"Um, it's the name of a sandwich."],[171.51,"I'm joking. Uh yeah, it is."],[176.87,"I love a good Reuben sandwich."],[179.19,"Um. I will have to look it up."],[186.39,"Um I think it's connected to what's translated here as humiliation, but I don't think it quite means humiliation."],[200.35,"I grew up watching Star Wars."],[202.03,"Yeah, I was uh So yeah."],[208.99,"Uh your mileage may vary."],[213.55,"Um and for the record, uh Leia, even though she doesn't get a lot of attention as a person in the rest of the Old Testament, is a saint in the Orthodox Church."],[230.51,"There are icons of her."],[234.07,"And sadly, in English, the Greek is more like righteous Leia."],[242.55,"But a lot of the English icons of her say just Leia."],[247.99,"Of course, righteous and just be the same thing, but it also, when you look at it, it sounds like it's saying just Leah."],[253.59,"It's kind of like, seriously, guys, have you not read the story?"],[258.23,"Come on. Yeah."],[262.87,"Yeah, yeah. Verse thirty three, then she conceived again and bore Jacob a second son."],[272.55,"And said, Because the Lord heard I was hated, he has therefore given me this son also."],[276.79,"So she called his name Simeon"],[281.07,"She conceived again and bore a son and said, Now this time my husband will be on my side, because I have borne him three sons, therefore she called his name Levi."],[291.71,"Now she conceived again and bore a son and said, Now I will give thanks to the Lord, therefore she called his name Judah, then she stopped bearing."],[302.35,"So Reuben and Simeon will read more about later."],[307.07,"Things don't necessarily go so well later in their lives."],[311.11,"But notice Levi, from whom the priesthood will be descended, Judah, through whom David and the kings of Judah will be descended, are sons of Leah, not of Rachel."],[330.95,"Worth noting. Chapter 30, verse one."],[337.75,"Now when Rachel saw that she bore Jacob no children, Rachel envied her sister and said to Jacob, Give me children, or else I die."],[349.67,"If I don't have a baby soon, I will die."],[355.99,"Notice how this weird reversal has happened now."],[360.72,"Probably until this point for their whole lives, Leah had probably envied Rachel."],[369.24,"And Rachel is the wife who their husband loves."],[373.9,"But now it's Rachel who envies Leah."],[375.9,"Why? Because as we saw, God intervened to make things right."],[386.38,"Verse 2, so Jacob's anger was aroused against Rachel, and he said, Am I in the place of God who has withheld from you the fruit of the womb?"],[399.34,"Remember how I said that maybe things aren't going to go so swell with this whole dynamic?"],[404.26,"Uh Jacob is basically like blaming God."],[412.68,"Don't talk to me, talk to God."],[415.26,"I've been saying, because remember, there is no concept of male infertility."],[419.02,"But even if he did have that concept, he's the one who's been getting Leah pregnant."],[425.88,"But Jacob is just straight out blaming God."],[429.01,"You have an issue with God."],[430.29,"I didn't do anything."],[432.03,"When as we've seen, all of this is actually based on what Jacob has been doing and how he's been treating Leah and how he's been treating Rachel."],[445.39,"Verse 3, she replied to Jacob, Here is my maid Bilhah, go into her, and she will bear on my knees that I also may. have children by her"],[457.51,"She then gave him Bilhah, her maid, as wife, and Jacob went into her."],[464.23,"Who's this remind you of?"],[466.55,"Sarah? Hagar. Oh, take my."],[473.89,"How did that go?"],[476.13,"Not well. Not well."],[478.13,"Right in Abraham's family."],[481.41,"You see, this also is not gonna go so swell."],[487.94,"Oh, and notice Jacob, like Abraham, is just sort of compliant."],[493.06,"Oh, third wife, okay."],[503.18,"Thus Bilhah, Rachel's handmaiden, conceived and bore Jacob a son."],[508.54,"Then Rachel said, God has judged me, and he has heard my voice and given me a son."],[513.5,"Therefore she called his name Dan."],[518.22,"Let me just tell you now."],[520.54,"Nothing good is gonna come out of Dan or the tribe of Dan."],[527.98,"This is this is gonna, I mean, this is we just came from Revelation."],[534.48,"Looped back around to Genesis."],[535.92,"Remember, Dan is the tribe that gets left off in the listing of the twelve tribes in Revelation."],[541.68,"So just use that as a keystone"],[545.4,"What's going to happen with that?"],[546.44,"But this is how it starts."],[551.28,"And Bilha's son counts as Rachel's son."],[555.92,"Sort of, yes."],[558.4,"Rachel feels like it should."],[561.04,"Yes. Rachel feels like that's that's how uh this should be."],[570.48,"But notice, notice."],[573.36,"It's not just that this is like third wife or handmaiden."],[577.76,"How is this framed?"],[580.96,"Jacob says, God is the one stopping you from. having a child, Rachel"],[588.92,"And Rachel comes up with a plan to do what?"],[593.56,"Get around God."],[601.4,"She doesn't like go and repent."],[605.16,"She doesn't go and pray."],[608.28,"Say, God, I don't know what I did, whatever, but please let me have a child."],[618.73,"She tries to get around God through her own ingenuity."],[622.81,"And you get damned."],[632.53,"Now Rachel's handmaiden Bilha conceived again and bore Jacob a second son."],[637.09,"Then Rachel said, God has helped me, and I have wrestled with my sister, and indeed I have prevailed."],[643.89,"So she called his name naphtali."],[648.93,"Another one of the far northern tribes who things aren't going to go so swell with."],[660.69,"I beat my I got my sister."],[663.89,"This is healthy."],[665.03,"These are good family dynamics."],[670.12,"Verse 9. Now when Leah saw she had stopped bearing, she took Zilpah, her handmaiden, and gave her to Jacob as a wife."],[680.96,"Wife number four."],[685.68,"So Jacob went into her."],[689.04,"And Zilpa, Leah's handmaiden, conceived and bore Jacob a son."],[692.32,"Then Leah said, Good fortune."],[695.44,"Thus she called his name Gad."],[699.36,"Now Zilpa, Leah's handmaid, bore Jacob a second son."],[703.12,"Then Leah said, I am blessed."],[705.36,"For the women shall call me blessed."],[707.2,"So she called his name Asher."],[715.68,"So we're now up to eight by my count."],[718.88,"There's gonna be some more"],[726.36,"Yeah. But you can see now this has become rather than the occasion of anyone repenting or anyone trying to sort out the family dynamics or Jacob getting his act together."],[743.0,"This has just be cut turned into this weird rivalry."],[748.49,"Of who could get the most kids by hook or crook."],[753.73,"Now Reuben went in the days of wheat harvest and found mandrakes in the field and brought them to his mother Leia."],[759.73,"Thus Rachel said to Leah, give me some of your son's mandrakes."],[763.77,"But she said to her, Is it a small matter that you would take away that you have taken away my husband?"],[769.45,"Would you take away my son's mandrakes also?"],[773.45,"So Rachel said, Not so, let him lie with you tonight for your son's mandrakes."],[780.57,"Okay, so he finds some wild mandrakes."],[782.81,"Rachel wants some."],[792.9,"She says, o,kay you can sleep with him tonight instead of me."],[797.78,"If I could have some of the mandrakes."],[803.87,"We're 16 now."],[805.07,"W Jhenacob came. out of the field in the evening, Leah went out to meet him and said, You must come in to me, for I have surely hired you with my son's mandrakes"],[812.99,"So he lay with her that night."],[814.91,"This is a grooming prize."],[816.83,"Yeah, yeah. Or just prostitution for mandrakes."],[820.67,"I don't know."],[821.15,"Male prostitution for mandrakes."],[823.95,"I heard something body uh talking about this paper because it's like why mandrakes, but uh apparently there was like considered an aphrodisiac."],[832.59,"Yeah. Yes, yeah."],[835.47,"And so, okay, so yes, we should explain that."],[839.07,"Yeah. These mandrakes were c were, yeah, considered an aphrodisiac."],[844.43,"You can't even tell that it's a little rubber."],[847.15,"Yeah. It was more of a used as a sexual stimulant."],[850.11,"a Um so you'll find lot of commentary on this."],[860.47,"Um Jewish and patristic."],[864.07,"Uh, when they comment on this, they talk about um this showing that Rachel had a certain lasciviousness that she was putting um and this may have been related to why she isn't conceiving that she was more focused on the pleasure of the sexual act than on having children."],[895.71,"Is that why I said he loved her more?"],[898.91,"Maybe, yeah. Part of that's just he's more attracted to her, as we've seen."],[903.71,"But yeah, maybe he finds that more enjoyable."],[907.71,"Because clearly he was, even though she wasn't having children, he was still sleeping with her rather than Leia most of the time."],[914.77,"That's why Leia had to sort of bargain to get a night with him."],[917.97,"Well, in the early modern and medieval world, maybe in ancient world too, yeah."],[927.89,"If you have more fun in your sex, you're more likely to have children."],[933.33,"It was actually the opposite."],[936.21,"Yes. In the ancient world, yeah this I really don't want to get too graphic, but in the ancient world they thought that if a woman enjoyed herself that was flush that would flush out the womb."],[954.09,"Oh god. And I'm trying not to be graphic."],[957.21,"That would flush out the womb and she wouldn't get pregnant."],[962.57,"Yeah. So that that is part of why there was this correlation between right pursuing the one or pursuing the other."],[977.98,"And yeah. And so you would then culturally look down on the person who's just out for pleasure and not for children."],[994.02,"Verse seventeen, thus God listened to Leah, and she conceived and bore Jacob a fifth son."],[1000.1,"Then Leah said, God has given me my wages, because I have given my handmaiden to my husband."],[1005.86,"So she called his name Issachar."],[1009.14,"Now Leah conceived again and bore Jacob a sixth son."],[1012.66,"Then Leah said, God has endowed me with a good endowment."],[1016.1,"Now my husband will choose me, because I have borne him six sons."],[1020.26,"So she called his name Zebulun."],[1022.58,"Afterwards she bore a daughter and called her name Dinah."],[1026.26,"I know technically it's Dinah, but again."],[1029.3,"Um The Dinah Shore show."],[1030.86,"Come on. That's it."],[1034.62,"So Leia ends up with six sons and a daughter."],[1038.06,"We've got four more sons from the two handmaidens."],[1040.86,"We're up to ten sons and a daughter."],[1043.43,"And so this thing with God honoring her is related to what we were just talking about."],[1049.45,"The idea that Leia is showing by this that she wants to have more children."],[1055.39,"And isn't concerned about the other so much."],[1057.55,"And therefore, God honors the fact that she wants to have more children by giving her more children is the idea."],[1064.99,"Is Rachel a saint in the church?"],[1067.47,"Yes. Yes, she is."],[1071.79,"But we'll see."],[1072.51,"Some interesting things happen with Rachel"],[1075.75,"Rachel becomes one of the clearest cases of someone after they're dead praying for their descendants in the Old Testament."],[1084.07,"Not the only case, but one of the clearest cases."],[1088.79,"So she literally does saint things within the pages of the Old Testament."],[1096.55,"So verse 22."],[1098.79,"Then God remembered Rachel, and God listened to her and opened her womb."],[1103.75,"Thus she conceived and bore a son and said, God has taken away my reproach."],[1108.55,"So she called his name Joseph and said, The Lord shall add another son to me."],[1114.71,"Now we're up to 11."],[1116.31,"And here's Joseph who, will be.come important, as we'll see later on"],[1122.83,"Now it came to pass when Rachel had borne Joseph that Jacob said to Laban, Send me away that I may go to my own place and to my country."],[1131.15,"Give me my wives and my children for whom I have served you, and let me go, for you know the service I rendered you."],[1145.71,"Let's set him there for a few days while Esau cools down."],[1150.91,"So this has been fourteen years, plus the time it took to have twelve children, albeit from four wives."],[1162.96,"So we're probably talking at least 22 years, maybe more like 25 years."],[1169.84,"He's been there with Laban a long time, and he now has his own very large extended family."],[1177.04,"So at this point, he's like, okay, I'm ready to head back to Canaan now."],[1182.16,"After all this time has passed."],[1187.44,"Verse 27, then Laban said to him, If I could find grace in your eyes, I would seek for it divinely, for God has blessed me by your coming."],[1196.24,"So he said, name me your wages and I will give it."],[1199.86,"So Laban says, Hey, no, it's been really good having you here."],[1202.91,"God has blessed me while you've been here."],[1205.85,"I don't want you to leave yet."],[1208.01,"What what'll it cost me to keep you here?"],[1210.51,"What's the contract negotiations."],[1213.76,"What do I need to do?"],[1214.96,"What do I need to offer you for you to stay?"],[1220.24,"Verse 29, Jacob replied, You know how I have served you and how numerous your cattle became with me."],[1226.08,"For what you had before I came was little and it is increased to a great amount."],[1230.4,"The Lord has blessed you since my coming."],[1232.72,"Now, therefore, when shall I also establish my own house?"],[1237.68,"So he's saying, Look, Uncle Laban, yeah."],[1240.72,"It has been good for you, especially."],[1244.45,"Me being here."],[1245.65,"You're doing great."],[1247.73,"I want to take care of my own business now."],[1248.77,"I got wives"],[1252.06,"I'm an adult."],[1254.94,"I got tons of kids."],[1256.94,"I need to get my own thing going."],[1261.34,"Verse 31, thus Laban said to him, What shall I give you?"],[1266.46,"Jacob replied, You shall not give me anything."],[1269.74,"If you will do this thing for me, I will again feed and keep your sheep."],[1274.62,"Let me pass through all your flocks today, removing from them all the gray sheep and all the spotted and speckled among the goats, and these shall be my wages."],[1286.06,"So my righteousness will answer for me in time to come."],[1289.06,"When the subject of my wages comes before you, everyone that is not speckled. and spotted among the goats and gray among the sheep will be considered stolen if it is with me"],[1299.78,"Okay. So he says, okay, I'll make you a deal."],[1304.36,"I'll keep your sheep for a while more."],[1307.58,"But all the ones that are spotted, speckled, aren't pure white among the sheep and the goats belong to me when I take my leave."],[1319.0,"Those will be my, that'll be my share of the herds."],[1321.88,"And everything that's clean, plain white."],[1326.06,"Which would be the ones that would be considered the best."],[1329.03,"So I'll take all the quasi-defective ones."],[1331.51,"I'll leave you all the good ones."],[1333.35,"And he says, and you'll be. able to judge whether I'm trying to pull something, because you could just come look at my herd"],[1340.11,"And if you see any in there that aren't spottled or speckled or anything, those are stolen."],[1345.95,"You can have them back."],[1349.84,"Then Laban said to him, Let it be according to your word."],[1353.04,"So he agrees to those terms."],[1355.04,"So he removed that day all the male goats that were speckled and spotted, all the female goats that were speckled and spottled, spotted, everyone that had some white in it, and all the gray ones among the sheep, and gave them into the hands of his sons."],[1368.08,"Then he put three days' journey between himself and Jacob, and Jacob fed the rest of Laban's flocks."],[1375.6,"Now Jacob took for himself rods of green poplar and of the almond and chestnut trees, peeled white strips in them, tearing off the bark, so the white strips he had peeled appear he had peeled appeared on the rods as spotted."],[1390.36,"Then he placed the rods he had peeled in the gutters of the watering troughs where the flocks came to drink, so they should conceive at the rods as they came to drink."],[1399.96,"So the flocks conceived before the rods, and the flocks brought forth speckled, spotted, and ash colored speckled."],[1406.6,"But Jacob separated the male lambs and placed a speckled ram before the sheep, and all that were spotted among the male lambs."],[1413.72,"Then he separated for himself flocks by themselves, and did not mix them with the sheep of Laban."],[1420.12,"Thus it came to pass whenever the sheep conceived that Jacob placed the rods before the sheep in the gutters, so they might conceive according to the rods."],[1424.36,"But whenever the sheep had already given birth, he did not put them in"],[1430.72,"Thus it came to pass that the unmarked were Laban's and the marked were Jacob's."],[1434.56,"So the man became exceedingly rich and had many cattle and oxen, male and female servants, and camels and donkeys."],[1440.64,"So basically, Jacob now decides to try to outcon his con man uncle."],[1448.56,"And so he goes and he finds these particular branches, he strips them, he puts them in the watering troughs of the sheep, but the time is coming for them to conceive, so they're drinking it while the babies are gestating and things, and it causes them to have these blemishes."],[1466.08,"And he goes, Oh, look, another blemish."],[1468.24,"Oh, darn, this one's mine."],[1469.2,"s And so he end up shuffling off the vast majority, of the flocks and herds."],[1478.97,"And uh what do you think Jacob would claim to justify doing this?"],[1487.45,"Whatever he messed with me on that whole wife thing."],[1490.65,"So I'm just trying to make this right."],[1494.33,"Wig. And me getting rich is gonna make this right."],[1499.46,"So we can keep going a little bit."],[1504.5,"Now, Jacob heard the words of Laban's sons saying, Jacob has taken away all that was your father's, and from our father's property. he acquired all this wealth"],[1515.36,"So some of Laban's sons."],[1518.18,"Like the one the ones who are going to inherit Laban's stuff, who are going to take over this family, they start looking at Jacob's flocks and herds, and Laban's flocks of herds, knowing that Jacob is leaving."],[1530.42,"And they go to their dad and say, Hey, uh cousin."],[1536.82,"And I think he's pulling something."],[1539.03,"He seems to be taking all your stuff."],[1543.03,"So Jacob saw Laban's countenance, and indeed it was not favorable toward him as before."],[1548.71,"That's an understatement."],[1551.19,"Then the Lord said to Jacob, Return to your father's land and to your family, and I will be with you."],[1557.65,"So God is giving him the heads up to get out of Dodge."],[1563.85,"So Jacob sent and called Rachel and Leah to the field where the flocks were, and said to them, I see your father's countenance, but it is not favorable toward me as before."],[1574.33,"But the God of my father has been with me."],[1577.13,"Now you know that with all my might I served your father."],[1580.65,"Yet your father deceived me and changed my wages ten times with respect to the Baalayams, but God did not allow him to harm me."],[1590.09,"Now, did we hear anything about this?"],[1594.33,"No. He did change his wages in terms of wives."],[1597.85,"To Leah and Rachel"],[1598.61,"But Jacob may not want to bring that up."],[1605.57,"If he said thus, the speckled shall be your wages, then all the flocks bore speckled, but if he said thus, the white shall be your wages, then all the sheep bore white."],[1614.13,"So God has taken away all your father's cattle and given them to me."],[1617.89,"It had nothing to do with anything I did."],[1619.89,"It's just God wanted me to have all this."],[1631.65,"And behold, the male goats and the rams that were speckled, spotted, and ash colored, speckled, were mating with the sheep and the goats."],[1637.73,"And the angel of God spoke to me in a dream, saying, Jacob, thus I said, here I am."],[1642.21,"So he said, Lift your eyes and now and see all the male goats and the rams mating with the sheep, and the goats are speckled, spotted, ash colored, speckled."],[1649.37,"For I have seen everything Laban is doing to you."],[1652.01,"I am the God who appeared to you at Bethel where you anointed the pillar and made a vow to me."],[1656.17,"Now then arise, get out of this land, and return to the land of your nativity, and I will be with you."],[1681.13,"Yeah, the very last bit."],[1683.21,"The very last bit about leaving."],[1685.75,"Yeah, but that's not how the sheep got speckled."],[1687.15,"how the sheep got speckled. We just read"],[1694.24,"Jacob is saying, Oh, I don't know what God just wanted me to have all the sheep."],[1713.2,"Then Rachel and Leah answered and said to him, Is there still any portion or inheritance for us at our father's house?"],[1720.96,"That's really, do you leave him anything, Jacob?"],[1725.44,"Are you just taking literally all of his stuff?"],[1729.76,"Are we considered strangers by him?"],[1731.96,"For he sold us and also completely consumed our money."],[1741.32,"Now then, whatever God has said to you, do it."],[1746.81,"So what are they saying?"],[1749.13,"They're saying, yeah, we kind of know about the chicanery with him getting you to marry both of us."],[1757.61,"And how he treated us and all that."],[1760.49,"So, as far as we're concerned, all his stuff belongs to us and our kids anyway, so take it all."],[1770.25,"Alright. So we can see this as Laban getting his comeuppance, though, because, you know."],[1782.13,"I'm starting to really surprise Laban."],[1784.29,"He did he did try to con a con man, and seems like he got out conned."],[1793.09,"Then Jacob rose and set his sons and his wives on camels, and he'd carried away all his livestock and all his possessions acquired in Mesopotamia, everything belonging to him to go to his father Isaac and Canaan."],[1806.37,"Now Laban had gone to shear his sheep, and Rachel had stolen her father's idols."],[1812.77,"So it's not just, yeah, go take all his stuff."],[1815.97,"They went and took a bunch of his stuff."],[1820.35,"So they they went and took more of their dad's stuff on their way out."],[1826.16,"Including Rachel's case, these idols."],[1831.84,"Well, Nahor was."],[1837.12,"Laban may have been, among other things."],[1843.12,"So Laban's not a saint."],[1845.68,"No. But Jacob had hidden from Laban the Syrian his intention of running away."],[1855.06,"So he waits until Laban goes and takes all of his flocks to go get them sheared."],[1861.14,"And then he splits town."],[1866.38,"So he fled with all that he had and crossed the river and headed for the mountains of Gilead."],[1873.42,"Then Laban was told on the third day that Jacob had fled."],[1878.72,"So he finds out only three days later, because somebody has to go tell him."],[1883.57,"So he took all his brethren with him and pursued him for seven days' journey."],[1889.17,"And he overtook him in the mountains of Gilead."],[1892.45,"Now, how would he overtake him?"],[1893.81,"Well, just as he took his men."],[1895.57,"So he took his sons, his male servants."],[1898.71,"Whereas Jacob is traveling with his wives, his kids, herds, flocks, they're moving a lot slower."],[1908.07,"Still took him seven days."],[1913.27,"But God had come to Laban the Syrian in a dream by night and said to him, Be careful that you do not speak evil things to Jacob at any time."],[1922.39,"So Laban overtook Jacob."],[1924.15,"Now Jacob had pitched his tent in the mountains, and Laban with his brethren pitched in the mountains of Gilead."],[1929.75,"Then Laban said to Jacob, What have you done?"],[1933.19,"That you have stolen away unknown to me and robbed me and carried away my daughters like captives taken with the sword."],[1942.23,"You notice, you know, these two guys have alternating versions of reality, depending on."],[1948.76,"He now stole his daughters his captives."],[1951.08,"Like you.'re the one who tricked him into marrying both of them"],[1955.92,"And now you're accusing him of stealing them by violence."],[1959.04,"Like. Why did you flee away secretly and steal away from me and not tell me?"],[1965.89,"For I might have sent you away with joy and songs with timbrel and harp."],[1970.13,"And you did not allow me to kiss my sons and my daughters."],[1973.97,"Now you have done foolishly in so doing."],[1976.69,"It is in my power to do you harm, but the God of your fathers spoke to me last night, saying, Be careful that you do not speak evil things to Jacob at any time."],[1985.65,"Now notice how he phrases that the God of your father."],[1990.61,"Not God in general."],[1998.06,"Now you have surely gone because you greatly long for your father's house, but why did you steal my gods?"],[2006.87,"Good question. Good question."],[2012.79,"Uh there could be good reasons."],[2016.07,"I mean, there aren't."],[2017.03,"But there could like a good reason could be like, hey, you shouldn't be worshiping idols."],[2023.19,"You should worship the God of Abraham and Isaac."],[2026.15,"That's not what we're going to get."],[2027.59,"It's more likely it's that they were made out of like gold and silver and stuff."],[2031.43,"You know. But right."],[2034.03,"Um. Then Jacob answered and said to Laban, Because I was afraid, for I said, Perhaps you would take your daughters and all my possessions from me by force."],[2038.95,"Like, no you were gonna get violent and steal everything from me."],[2052.83,"Again, weird alternating views of reality."],[2056.43,"With whomever you find your gods, let him not live in the presence of our brethren."],[2060.91,"Identify what I have of yours and take it with you."],[2063.71,"For Jacob did not know that Rachel had stolen them."],[2068.35,"So he's like, hey, you find somebody here hanging on to your gods that they stole."],[2074.11,"You let me know, and I'll I'll take care of them, and you can have them back."],[2080.75,"Thus Laban went in and searched Leah's tent but found nothing."],[2082.67,"'s tent. Then he entered Rachel"],[2084.39,"Then he searched Jacob's and those of the handmaidens, but found nothing."],[2090.07,"Now Rachel had taken the idols, put them in the camel's saddle, and sat on them."],[2095.77,"So she's got them stashed."],[2097.79,"Underneath the saddle."],[2100.43,"Then she said to her father, Let it not displease my lord that I cannot rise before you, for the manner of women is with me."],[2108.03,"So he searched the entire tent but did not find the idols."],[2111.23,"That's euphemized a little bit."],[2113.15,"She's basically saying, Dad, I'd love to get off the camel and greet you, but it's my time of the month."],[2122.27,"So I can't get off this saddle."],[2124.75,"I have to stay sitting here on top of not your idols."],[2126.91,"Okay So now she's getting it on the act too."],[2133.13,"This is uh like uh the sting."],[2138.19,"Like used carbon anyway."],[2140.67,"Yeah, yeah, none of these people."],[2141.87,"Yeah, everyone in this story of Jacob is just like pushing the side of their nose continuously, I think."],[2146.59,"Like. Well, it's interesting that you say, like, they have conflict reality, but like they both assume the same things about each other."],[2154.27,"Yes. Yeah. Yeah."],[2155.87,"They do have the same things."],[2156.83,"And just sort of spin this elaborate, like no, that's not what's happening."],[2163.47,"What's happening is this fantastic tale."],[2166.75,"Yeah. Pointing at each other, yeah."],[2170.59,"Then Jacob was angry and rebuked Laban"],[2175.83,"And Jacob answered and said to Laban, What is my injustice?"],[2178.87,"What is my sin that you have so hotly pursued me?"],[2181.76,"Because now he's like, Oh, I see you falsely accused me."],[2187.01,"Although you searched all my things, what part of your household goods have you found?"],[2191.41,"Set them here before my brethren and your brethren, so that they so they may judge between us."],[2196.77,"These twenty years I have been with you."],[2198.93,"Your sheep and your female goats have not miscarried their young, and I have not eaten the rams of your flock."],[2204.53,"That which was caught by wild animals I did not bring to you."],[2207.73,"I bore the loss of any stolen by day or by night."],[2210.93,"There I was, in the day the drought consumed me, and the frost by night, and my sleep departed from my eyes, and I walked uphill both ways, and thus I have been in your house twenty years."],[2228.01,"I served you fourteen years for your two daughters, and six years for your flock, and you have changed my wages ten times with respect to the female lands."],[2237.47,"Ah, the airing of grievances."],[2241.71,"Look at how you mistreated me, Laban."],[2244.11,"How dare you, sir, come here and accuse me."],[2248.27,"Unless the God of my father Abraham and the fear of Isaac had been with me, surely now you would have sent me away empty-handed."],[2255.63,"But God saw my affliction and the labor of my hands and rebuked you last night."],[2265.03,"Then Laban answered and said to Jacob, These daughters are my daughters, and these sons are my sons, and these sheep are my sheep."],[2272.87,"All you see belongs to me and my daughters."],[2275.67,"But what can I do for them today or for the children they bore?"],[2279.11,"Now therefore come, let us make a covenant, you and I, and let it be a witness between you and me."],[2284.87,"Then he said, Look, there is no one with us."],[2287.43,"God himself is witness between you and me."],[2291.72,"So Laban sort of relents."],[2293.88,"He's like, actually, all this stuff is really mine."],[2297.32,"These are my daughters, the sons of my daughters, my flocks."],[2302.86,"But what what can I do?"],[2305.42,"You kind of got me over a barrel here."],[2308.47,"You win. So he says, at least let's make an agreement here before we part ways, and there's nobody else here, so God will be our witness."],[2318.49,"Let's at least make this an amicable separation."],[2322.01,"Stay away from me."],[2323.82,"From now on."],[2326.54,"So Jacob took a stone and set it up as a pillar."],[2329.98,"Then Jacob said to his brethren, Gather stones."],[2333.34,"So they took stones and made a heap, and they ate and drank there on the heap."],[2337.82,"And Laban said to him, This heap is a witness between you and me today."],[2342.86,"Laban called it the heap of testimony, but Jacob called it the witness heap."],[2348.82,"Which is a slight variation."],[2352.04,"But you have this big pile of stones, that they can point to and say."],[2361.54,"Then Laban said, This heap and this pillar are a witness between you and me this day."],[2366.98,"Therefore its name was called this heap witness."],[2373.22,"And also the vision, because he said, May God watch between you and me, but we are absent one from another."],[2380.26,"If you humble my daughters, or if you take other wives besides my daughters, although no man is with us, see God is witness between you and me."],[2389.07,"So Laban.'s saying, Look, I'm not going to be able to, but God's going to keep an eye on you"],[2395.35,"Don't you be taking other wives besides my daughters, although he already had."],[2402.47,"With the maidservants."],[2404.37,"And you don't mistreat them."],[2407.41,"Then Laban said to Jacob, Listen, this heap and pillar are a witness."],[2411.81,"This heap is a witness, and this pillar is a witness."],[2415.01,"Why does he keep reiterating this?"],[2416.61,"Well, that's two witnesses."],[2418.51,"You establish things."],[2419.63,"This is from later in the Torah, but you establish things by two witnesses."],[2425.15,"That I will not pass beyond this heap of this pillar to you, and you will not pass beyond this heap of this pillar to me for harm."],[2432.59,"This is the line"],[2436.63,"You come back across this point to Mesopotamia, there's gonna be a fight."],[2444.31,"And if I come over to your side of the line, there's gonna be a fight."],[2450.15,"So this is not a super amicable parting of the ways."],[2454.81,"I mean, it's better than having a fight right now."],[2457.29,"But they're basically saying, neither of us is gonna cross this line, and you better be good to my daughters."],[2468.09,"The God of Abraham and the God of Nahor judge between us"],[2468.21,"Yeah. Thus Jacob swore by the fear of his father Isaac."],[2478.29,"Then Jacob offered a sacrifice on the mountain and called his brethren, and they ate bread and drank and stayed all night on the mountain."],[2490.93,"He's basically he's swearing on his father's life and honor, is the idea."],[2499.81,"Because he's still alive."],[2503.1,"So the idea would be like if he breaks this oath, something bad would happen to his father."],[2513.18,"And if you do something bad to your father, that's like e-ticket to hell."],[2519.83,"That's like the worst thing you could do is like dishonor your own father that way."],[2525.95,"So that's the idea."],[2528.51,"Um swearing on the fear of his father, Isaac."],[2535.07,"So, yes. So tonight we had we did three whole chapters."],[2541.07,"Told you Old Testament was gonna go a little faster because it's stories."],[2544.67,"Uh, but this was the Laban evening."],[2547.23,"So we saw the Laban thing."],[2550.43,"Uh we saw Laban getting one over on Jacob after Jacob got one over on his father and brother."],[2558.35,"Then we saw Jacob's con man revenge, and finally, this uh not too. friendly separating of the ways"],[2569.09,"So as we leave off now, Jacob is no longer welcome with his mom's family."],[2576.21,"This means he's gonna have to go back to his dad and his brother Esau."],[2584.93,"So next time, next week, we'll pick up here in chapter 32, where Jacob and Esau are going to."],[2596.05,"Yeah. Jacob is gonna be getting ready to meet his his brother."],[2601.25,"And we're we're gonna see."],[2604.05,"This is we're we're gonna see the promised uh growth."],[2609.49,"That I promised the ar.k for Jacob and Esau that I promised at the beginning of this whole story"],[2616.57,"So thank you, everybody."],[2619.85,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2627.21,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2632.57,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":22.08,"lv":2,"h":"29:31 - The Lord opens Leah's womb","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"When the Lord saw Leah was <b>hated</b>, he opened her womb; Rachel was <b>barren</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God stepping in</b> to make the situation right</li><li class=\"d0\">Leah had <b>no say</b> - none of it her idea</li><li class=\"d1\">stuck for life with a husband who <b>doesn't love her</b>, married to the sister he does</li><li class=\"d0\">Ancient security = <b>children, especially sons</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>firstborn son</b> inherits when husband dies, secures his mother's future</li><li class=\"d0\">Children as <b>recompense</b> from God</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob might have read it as a message about <b>how he treated them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he's still sleeping with her - \"not that appalled by her\"</li></ul>"},{"t":142.58,"lv":3,"h":"29:32 - Reuben; Leah a saint","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Leah bears <b>Reuben</b>: \"The Lord has looked on my <b>humiliation</b>; now my husband will <b>love me</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"depressing and sad\" - \"now I've had his firstborn son, now he'll love me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Name: he'll have to look it up - maybe connected to the word translated humiliation, \"but I don't think it quite means humiliation\"; also \"the name of a sandwich\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Leah is a <b>saint in the Orthodox Church</b> - icons of her</li><li class=\"d1\">Greek: <b>righteous Leah</b>; English icons just say \"<b>Just Leah</b>\" - \"have you not read the story?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":262.87,"lv":3,"h":"29:33-35 - Simeon, Levi, Judah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Verse 33: second son <b>Simeon</b> - \"the Lord heard I was <b>hated</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Levi</b>: \"now my husband will be on my side\" - three sons</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Judah</b>: \"Now I will <b>give thanks</b> to the Lord\" - then she stopped bearing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reuben and Simeon</b>: things don't go so well later in their lives</li><li class=\"d0\">But <b>Levi</b> (<b>priesthood</b>) and <b>Judah</b> (<b>David</b> and kings of Judah) are Leah's sons, not Rachel's</li></ul>"},{"t":330.95,"lv":2,"h":"30:1-2 - Rachel envies Leah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 30:1</b>: Rachel bears no children, <b>envies her sister</b> - \"Give me children, or else I die\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Weird reversal</b>: Leah had probably envied Rachel all along, loved wife</li><li class=\"d1\">now Rachel envies Leah - because <b>God intervened</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Verse 2: Jacob angry - \"Am I in the place of God who has withheld the fruit of the womb?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Jacob <b>blaming God</b>: \"don't talk to me, talk to God\"</li><li class=\"d1\">no concept of <b>male infertility</b> - and he's getting Leah pregnant</li><li class=\"d1\">really based on <b>how Jacob treated</b> Leah and Rachel</li></ul>"},{"t":445.39,"lv":2,"h":"30:3-8 - Bilhah: Dan and Naphtali","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Rachel: \"Here is my maid <b>Bilhah</b>, she will bear <b>on my knees</b>\" - Jacob goes into her</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sarah and Hagar</b> - \"how did that go? Not well\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Jacob, like Abraham, just <b>compliant</b> - \"third wife, okay\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Son = <b>Dan</b>: \"God has judged me, heard my voice\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"nothing good\" from the <b>tribe of Dan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Dan is the tribe <b>left off the twelve in Revelation</b> - \"use that as a keystone\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Bilhah's son counts as <b>Rachel's</b> - sort of</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob said God withholds → Rachel's plan: <b>get around God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no repenting, no praying \"God, whatever I did\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>own ingenuity</b> - \"and you get damned\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Second son <b>Naphtali</b>: \"I have <b>wrestled</b> with my sister, and <b>prevailed</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">another far northern tribe, things won't go well</li><li class=\"d1\">\"healthy... good family dynamics\"</li></ul>"},{"t":670.12,"lv":3,"h":"30:9-13 - Zilpah: Gad and Asher","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Leah, having stopped bearing, gives <b>Zilpah</b> to Jacob - \"wife number four\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Son <b>Gad</b>: \"Good fortune\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Second son <b>Asher</b>: \"I am blessed; the women shall call me blessed\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Up to <b>eight</b> sons by his count - more coming</li><li class=\"d0\">No repentance, no sorting out family dynamics, no Jacob getting his act together</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>weird rivalry</b>: \"who could get the most kids by hook or crook\"</li></ul>"},{"t":753.73,"lv":2,"h":"30:14-16 - The mandrakes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Reuben finds <b>mandrakes</b> in wheat harvest, brings to Leah</li><li class=\"d0\">Rachel: give me some - Leah: \"Is it a small matter you have taken away <b>my husband</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Rachel: \"let him lie with you <b>tonight</b> for your son's mandrakes\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob comes in from field: Leah - \"I have surely <b>hired you</b> with my son's mandrakes\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he lay with her that night</li><li class=\"d0\">Why mandrakes? Considered an <b>aphrodisiac</b>, sexual stimulant</li><li class=\"d0\">Jewish and patristic commentary: Rachel's <b>lasciviousness</b> - maybe why she isn't conceiving</li><li class=\"d1\">focus on <b>pleasure</b> of the act, not on having children</li><li class=\"d0\">Leah had to <b>bargain for a night</b> - he was sleeping with Rachel most of the time</li></ul>"},{"t":917.97,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: pleasure and conceiving","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: more fun → more likely to have children? <b>Opposite</b> in the ancient world</li><li class=\"d1\">belief: if a woman enjoyed herself it would <b>flush out the womb</b> - no pregnancy</li><li class=\"d0\">Hence the correlation: pursuing the one or the other</li><li class=\"d0\">Culturally you'd <b>look down</b> on someone just out for <b>pleasure, not children</b></li></ul>"},{"t":994.02,"lv":2,"h":"30:17-21 - Issachar, Zebulun, Dinah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Fifth son <b>Issachar</b>: \"God has given me my <b>wages</b>, because I gave my handmaiden to my husband\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Sixth son <b>Zebulun</b>: \"a good endowment; now my husband will <b>choose me</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Daughter <b>Dinah</b> - \"the Dinah Shore show\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Leah: <b>six sons and a daughter</b>; four more from handmaidens → <b>ten sons and a daughter</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God honoring Leah: she <b>wants more children</b>, not concerned with the other</li><li class=\"d1\">God honors that by giving more</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Is Rachel a saint? <b>Yes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">one of the <b>clearest cases</b> in the OT of someone <b>after death praying for descendants</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"literally does saint things within the pages of the Old Testament\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1096.55,"lv":2,"h":"30:22-26 - Joseph; time to leave","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Verse 22: <b>God remembered Rachel</b>, opened her womb</li><li class=\"d0\">Son <b>Joseph</b>: \"God has taken away my reproach... the Lord shall add another son\"</li><li class=\"d1\">up to <b>eleven</b>; Joseph will become important</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob asks Laban to <b>send him away</b> - \"give me my wives and my children\"</li><li class=\"d1\">only meant to stay \"a few days while Esau cools down\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14 years</b> plus time to have twelve children → <b>22 to 25 years</b> with Laban</li><li class=\"d1\">now has his own <b>large extended family</b>; ready to head back to Canaan</li></ul>"},{"t":1187.44,"lv":2,"h":"30:27-34 - Negotiating the flocks","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Laban: \"God has <b>blessed me by your coming</b>\" - name your wages</li><li class=\"d1\">\"what do I need to offer you for you to stay?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob: your cattle <b>increased</b> since I came - \"when shall I establish <b>my own house</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm an adult, tons of kids, need my own thing going\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Verse 31: \"You shall not give me anything\" - the deal</li><li class=\"d1\">remove all <b>gray sheep, spotted and speckled goats</b> - <b>these are my wages</b></li><li class=\"d1\">plain white = the best → Jacob takes the \"quasi-defective ones\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"my <b>righteousness</b> will answer for me\" - Laban can check; any unmarked in his herd = <b>stolen</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Laban: \"Let it be according to your word\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1353.04,"lv":3,"h":"30:35-43 - Jacob's rods","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Laban removes the speckled and spotted, gives them to <b>his sons</b>; puts <b>three days' journey</b> between them</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob peels <b>rods</b> of poplar, almond, chestnut - white strips; places in <b>watering troughs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">flocks conceive before the rods → <b>speckled, spotted</b> young</li><li class=\"d0\">Separates his flocks; rods only for the stronger breeding</li><li class=\"d1\">unmarked = Laban's, marked = Jacob's; <b>exceedingly rich</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Jacob decides to <b>outcon his con man uncle</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"oh, look, another blemish... darn, this one's mine\"</li><li class=\"d0\">His justification? <b>Making right</b> the wife thing - \"me getting rich is gonna make this right\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1504.5,"lv":2,"h":"31:1-3 - Time to get out of Dodge","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 31</b>: Laban's sons: Jacob took <b>all our father's wealth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">heirs watching Jacob's flocks, knowing he's leaving</li><li class=\"d0\">Laban's <b>countenance</b> not favorable - \"an understatement\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Lord</b>: \"Return to your father's land... <b>I will be with you</b>\" - \"heads up\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1563.85,"lv":3,"h":"31:4-16 - Jacob and his wives","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jacob calls Rachel and Leah to the field</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Your father <b>changed my wages ten times</b>\" - God did not allow him to harm me</li><li class=\"d1\">we heard of wives only - \"may not want to bring that up\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Speckled/white wages - flocks bore accordingly: \"God has taken away your father's cattle\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"nothing to do with anything I did\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Dream: <b>angel of God</b> - the rams mating; \"I am the God who appeared at <b>Bethel</b>, where you anointed the pillar and made a vow\"</li><li class=\"d1\">arise, return to the land of your nativity</li><li class=\"d1\">aside: that's not how the sheep got speckled - Jacob: \"God just wanted me to have all the sheep\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Rachel and Leah: \"Is there still any <b>portion or inheritance</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"do you leave him anything, Jacob?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">father <b>sold us</b>, consumed our money - \"whatever God said, do it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"all his stuff belongs to us and our kids anyway\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Laban got <b>outconned</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1793.09,"lv":2,"h":"31:17-24 - Flight, pursuit, God's warning","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jacob puts sons and wives on <b>camels</b>, takes all livestock for Isaac in Canaan</li><li class=\"d0\">Laban gone to <b>shear sheep</b> - <b>Rachel stole her father's idols</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they also took \"more of their dad's stuff on the way out\"; Laban's not a saint</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob hid his intention; <b>crossed the river</b>, headed for <b>mountains of Gilead</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Laban told on the <b>third day</b>; pursues <b>seven days</b> with brethren</li><li class=\"d1\">he has sons and servants; Jacob slowed by wives, kids, herds</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God to Laban in a dream</b>: \"Be careful you do not speak evil things to Jacob\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1929.75,"lv":3,"h":"31:25-35 - Laban's search for the gods","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Laban: \"stolen away... carried off my daughters <b>like captives taken with the sword</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>alternating versions of reality</b>\" - Jacob tricked him into marrying both</li><li class=\"d0\">\"I might have sent you away with <b>joy and songs</b>, timbrel and harp\"; not allowed to kiss sons and daughters</li><li class=\"d0\">\"In my power to do you harm\" - but <b>the God of your father</b> spoke - not God in general</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Why did you steal my <b>gods</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not concern about idolatry - more likely <b>gold and silver</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob: afraid you'd take daughters by force - \"whoever has your gods <b>shall not live</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">didn't know Rachel stole them</li><li class=\"d0\">Laban searches Leah's tent, Jacob's, handmaids', then <b>Rachel's</b></li><li class=\"d1\">idols in the <b>camel's saddle</b>, she sits on them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"cannot rise... the manner of women is with me\" - \"time of the month\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Everyone in this story... pushing the side of their nose\" - they assume the same things about each other</li></ul>"},{"t":2170.59,"lv":3,"h":"31:36-42 - Jacob airs his grievances","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jacob angry: \"What is my injustice, my sin?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"what have you found of your household goods?\" - set it before the brethren to judge</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Twenty years</b>: no miscarriages, ate none of the rams, bore the losses to wild animals and thieves</li><li class=\"d1\">drought by day, frost by night - \"walked uphill both ways\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>14 years for two daughters, 6 for flock</b>; wages changed <b>ten times</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Airing of grievances\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Unless <b>the God of Abraham, fear of Isaac</b> was with me - \"sent me away empty-handed\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God saw affliction, <b>rebuked you last night</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2265.03,"lv":2,"h":"31:43-55 - The heap of witness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Laban: \"daughters are my daughters... sheep are my sheep\" - \"what can I do?\" - covenant, <b>God is witness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he relents - \"you got me over a barrel... you win\"; amicable separation</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob sets up <b>a pillar</b>, brethren gather stones, <b>heap</b>, eat on the heap</li><li class=\"d1\">Laban: Laban: <b>heap of testimony</b>; Jacob: <b>witness heap</b> - \"slight variation\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"May God watch between you and me\" - don't humble my daughters or take <b>other wives</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"although he already had\" - with the maidservants</li><li class=\"d0\">Heap and pillar = <b>two witnesses</b> - established by two witnesses, later in Torah</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>The line</b>: neither crosses \"for harm\" → fight if either does</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not a super amicable parting\" - \"you better be good to my daughters\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God of Abraham and of Nahor</b> judge between us</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob swears by <b>the fear of his father Isaac</b>, offers sacrifice, they eat bread on the mountain</li><li class=\"d1\">swearing on father's <b>life and honor</b> - he's still alive</li><li class=\"d1\">harming/dishonoring your father = \"e-ticket to hell\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2535.07,"lv":2,"h":"Wrap-up: the Laban chapters","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Three whole chapters\" tonight - OT goes faster, <b>stories</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>Laban evening</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Laban gets one over on Jacob, after Jacob got one over on father and brother</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jacob's con man revenge</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not-too-friendly <b>separating of ways</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob <b>no longer welcome</b> with his mom's family → must go back to <b>father and Esau</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>Genesis 32</b> - Jacob getting ready to meet <b>Esau</b>; promised growth"});
